\begin{ex}
Consider the functions $f(x) = x + 1$, and $g(x) = 2x$. Since
$(\comp{f}{g})(x) = g(f(x))$, for each input~$x$ you must first take
its successor, then multiply the result by two. So their composition
is given by $(\comp{f}{g})(x) = 2(x+1)$.
\end{ex}

